<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR firmer in all maturities.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR firmer in all maturities.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were firmer in all maturities after spot rates climbed higher on tight domestic liquidity, traders said.</p>
<p>Overnight and termed rates rose as more money flowed out of the system because Treasury bill awards were higher than the amounts on maturing bills.</p>
<p>Traders expected the situation to ease next week as some reverse repos mature.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			 SEPT 24		 SEPT 23</p>
<p>    1 W		12  3/4		 12 3/8</p>
<p>    2 W		12  9/16		12 5/16</p>
<p>    1 M		12  3/8		 12 3/16</p>
<p>    2 M		12  1/16		11 15/16</p>
<p>    3 M		11  7/8		 11 13/16</p>
<p>    6 M		12			11 7/8</p>
<p>    12M		12  1/8		 12 1/16</p>
<p>    DATE	     24-Sep		  23-Sep</p>
<p>    VAL		25-Sep		  24-Sep</p>
